.claude/plans/PLAN-166/archive/codex-r7-stophook-2135.md:11325:  On a `--link` rerun after a copy-installed SPEC or marker has been replaced by a symlink, the prior manifest contains only HASH rows, so this early success bypasses target validation. The continuity branch then marks the destination delivered and records the arbitrary live symlink as a trusted LINK entry. Require the live type to agree with the prior record rather than treating the absence of a LINK row as a match.
